<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21277] sanity-hsm test_606: mds1 not restarted after cleanup umount fails, test_607b hangs</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21277</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;sanity-hsm test_606 stops mds1, mounts the MDT device directly as ldiskfs/zfs, and registers a single EXIT trap: unmount_fstype mds1; start mds1 .... If that umount fails (EBUSY), set -e aborts the trap before start mds1 runs, so MDT0000 stays down. The next test, test_607b, then hangs until the test session times out (24 h here).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Fix: split the cleanup into separate stack_trap commands. First retry the umount for up to 60 s, then run unmount_fstype mds1 || true, then start mds1. A failed umount can then no longer skip the restart, and unmount_zfs still restores the dataset mountpoint property.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment>&amp;nbsp;&amp;lt;distro/arch&amp;gt;, &amp;lt;zfs|ldiskfs&amp;gt;</environment>
